{
  "task.5F4329B9065D310B.title": "Serenity, Mirage, or Wayfinder",
  "quest.2689B0928FA18765.quest_desc": [
    "The &aNova 77/HX&r is the last weapon in &eLTXI&r and the only one built on a Real Virtuality Processor.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"It costs 250M FE in the \", {\"text\": \"Fabricator\", \"color\": \"dark_green\"}, \", so charge your power storage before you start the craft. The \", {\"text\": \"Nova\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,ltxi:guide,ltxi:weapons/nova.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Nova page in the LTXI GuideMe\"}}, \" GuideMe page has the details.\"]",
    "",
    "The &6Feed The Beast&r challenge needs one as well: Against Causality builds a Nova into the Causal Anchor.",
  ],
  "quest.2618CDD301362A21.title": "Digital Smelting",
  "quest.507B07726C49351E.quest_desc": [
    "The Fabricator pulls ingredients from your inventory, which is fine for one turret and painful for forty circuits.",
    "",
    "The &aAuto Fabricator&r has 16 input slots and runs one recipe on repeat. Right-click a recipe in the Fabricator to write it onto an &2Empty Fabrication Blueprint&r, put the blueprint in the Auto Fabricator and pipe the ingredients in.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: Blueprints also work as patterns in an &eAE2&r Pattern Provider, but only while the Auto Fabricator's blueprint slot is empty.",
  ],
  "quest.1BD3EA2ADBDA309B.title": "Echo Serum",
  "quest.5417AFD81227465D.title": "Grinder",
  "quest.03BB4ADCCC53708D.quest_desc": [
    "Like tungsten, &aRhenium&r has no ore. This one is hiding in copper.",
    "",
    "When the &2ElectroCentrifuge&r turns a Copper Shard into a Crystal, it has a 6% chance to drop &aRhenium(VII) Oxide&r. The &2Chem Lab&r takes it through Ammonia to Ammonium Perrhenate, then to dust with Hydrogen, and the Arc Furnace melts the dust down under Argon.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The Real Virtuality Processor needs eight ingots, and each ingot takes two Oxides, so send all your copper through the full chain.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: &2Ammonia&r comes from Nitrogen and Hydrogen in the Chem Lab, or 200 mB at a time from grinding Crimson or Warped Fungus.",
  ],
  "quest.7731A2CFF3B9769C.title": "Fluoropolymer",
  "quest.59E5B7EF32280569.title": "Bio/ARU Garden",
  "quest.4382135A655314AF.quest_desc": [
    "The &aMixer&r combines items with fluids. Its first job is &2Sulfuric Acid&r, from Acidic Biomass and water.",
    "",
    "Later it makes Polymer Bars, Chorus Extract and Echo Serum as well, so a second Mixer pays off once the acid is flowing.",
  ],
  "quest.5E72E067E7C37D7D.quest_desc": [
    "While you're in the End, look down. &aNiobium Ore&r sits in the End Stone of the outer islands, and the End is the only place it generates.",
    "",
    "Mine a good amount and press some ingots into &aNiobium Plates&r in the &2Material Press&r. The High-Energy Voltaic Cell takes plates, and the Nano Logic Core takes Niobium Dust from the Grinder.",
    "",
    "Once you have a few ingots, &eProductive Bees&r and &eMystical Agriculture&r both have a niobium option, so the End trips don't have to last forever.",
  ],
  "quest.1BD6D491EEC018D0.quest_desc": [
    "The &aWonderland&r suit is &eLTXI&r's armor, and in this pack it comes out of the &6FTB Fabricator&r, not the LTXI one. Its recipes unlock once you've freed the End with your Skyline built.",
    "",
    "Each piece comes with a rank 1 &bBubble Projection Unit&r already fitted, worth 5 shield. Fabricate higher ranks and install them at the &3Upgrade Station&r, up to rank 4 for 20 shield per piece. Damage drains the shield before it reaches you, and it recharges on its own.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Check the \", {\"text\": \"Wonderland Armor\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,ltxi:guide,ltxi:armor.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the armor page in the LTXI GuideMe\"}}, \" GuideMe page for more details.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.21C4EB4528C091CA.title": "Geo Synthesizer",
  "quest.7731A2CFF3B9769C.quest_desc": [
    "&aFluoropolymer Bars&r go into nearly everything from here on, including the next circuit board, the bigger Voltaic Cell and the &6Wonderland Armor&r.",
    "",
    "Make a few in the &2Chem Lab&r and press one into a &aFluoropolymer Sheet&r. Each of its three fluids comes from a different place. &2Methane&r is the swamp Scrubber. &2Chlorine&r comes out of the ElectroCentrifuge from Sea Water or kelp. &2Hydrofluoric Acid&r is Fluorite in Sulfuric Acid, also in the Chem Lab.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: The Titanium Dust only acts as a catalyst and is never used up, and every craft leaves 1,000 mB of &2Hydrochloric Acid&r behind. Keep it, because the last step of the ore chain runs on it.",
  ],
  "quest.359C9BCF250CA832.title": "Welcome to &eLTX Industries&r!",
  "quest.2E5E8A019A56881E.quest_desc": [
    "The &dAssembler&r makes the parts the rest of the mod is built from, such as circuits, Voltaic Cells, machine housings and tech parts. The machines themselves are still crafted by hand or in the &dFabricator&r.",
    "",
    "It is also generally cheaper to craft items via the &dAssembler&r than manually.",
    "",
    "For now, you should make some &3Enhanced Circuits&r to move on to the next progression tier.",
  ],
  "quest.465A125AA3B84877.title": "Top-Rank Upgrades",
  "quest.465A125AA3B84877.quest_desc": [
    "With both top circuits in hand, the last ranks of the upgrade tree open up in the &2Fabricator&r.",
    "",
    "- &aΣ/VM3 Power Supply Unit&r: rank 4 needs a Nano-Core Processor and rank 5 a Real Virtuality Processor.",
    "- &2Bubble Projection Unit&r: ranks 3 and 4 need Nano-Core Processors, for 20 shield per Wonderland piece.",
    "- &aOverclocked Harvest Matrix&r: Fortune for tools, up to rank 5.",
    "- &2Combat Yield Protocol&r: Looting for weapons, up to rank 5.",
    "- &aFantasia Rulebook&r: creative flight on the Wonderland chestplate. It costs a Real Virtuality Processor and 150M FE.",
  ],
  "quest.6D7ED2315F9E93BD.title": "Voltaic Cell",
  "quest.5EF4EC94EEE9FCDB.quest_desc": [
    "Three quest paths come together here. The &aNano-Core Processor&r is tier 4, and it opens the Noctis turret, the Daybreak, the Bathyal Water Tank and rank 4 of most upgrades.",
    "",
    "Build it in the &2Assembler&r. Besides the Nano Logic Core and the cell it takes two Elite Boards, two Precision Circuits and eight &2Chorus Extract&r, which the Mixer makes from Chorus Fruit and Sulfuric Acid.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The Real Virtuality Processor takes four, so set the Assembler up to repeat it.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: Rhenium comes from the last step of the copper ore chain, and that step needs the &3Ore Crystallizing Tubes&r upgrade in the ElectroCentrifuge. It needs a Nano-Core Processor of its own, so build that upgrade next.",
  ],
  "quest.06354FA695904AFD.quest_desc": [
    "Plates and gears for metals and materials come from the &aMaterial Press&r. You'll need it soon, since the &3Upgrade Station&r takes Slatesteel Plates and only this machine makes them.",
    "",
    "Later on it is also the only way to make Niobium, Rhenium and Tungsten-Plated Slatesteel Plates.",
  ],
  "quest.781E24BC6FCF69AF.quest_desc": [
    "&2Argon&r is the one gas you can't get at home. A Scrubber only finds it in the End, on Ambient Gases.",
    "",
    "Bring back a bucket and fuse your first &aLogic Core&r in the &2Arc Furnace&r on Inert Gas Smelting. Every circuit from here on starts with Logic Cores, and Rhenium and the Nano Logic Core use Argon too.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: The End Scrubber also turns up the odd &2Chorus Extract&r. Keep them, since the Nano-Core Processor takes eight.",
  ],
  "quest.12991E755825749C.quest_desc": [
    "&aSulfuric Acid&r goes into &2Polymer Bars&r, which you need for your first Voltaic Cells.",
    "",
    "The &2Chem Lab&r also uses 125 mB of it for every Chunk it turns into Shards in the ore processing chain, so keep a tank of it next to that machine.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: Once you have an &2Atmospheric Scrubber&r in the Nether, its Ambient Gases mode collects Sulphurine, which the Chem Lab turns into acid with water and no berries.",
  ],
  "quest.03BB4ADCCC53708D.title": "Rhenium",
  "quest.5417AFD81227465D.quest_desc": [
    "A &aGrinder&r is a basic machine that breaks down items and raw materials into dusts or extra resources that can be further processed in other machines.",
    "",
    "In &2Element Extraction&r mode it pulls elements out of materials, such as Carbon Dust from coal and Acidic Biomass from Vitriol Berries.",
    "",
    "In &2Dye Extraction&r mode it grinds plants into dyes. Both modes are always available from the mode button, and recipes like bones into Bone Meal need no mode at all.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: the machine stays on whatever mode you left it in, so give each mode its own Grinder rather than switching back and forth.",
  ],
  "quest.2BDF212C585D1A2C.quest_desc": [
    "For metals, &eLTXI&r's ore processing chain runs through five machines.",
    "",
    "&a1)&r &aGrinder&r crushes raw ore into &2Dirty Dust",
    "&22)&r &2HydroSieve&r washes it into a &aClump",
    "&33)&r &3Voltaic Injector&r energizes it into a &aChunk",
    "&d4)&r &dChem Lab&r turns it into a &aShard",
    "&65)&r &6ElectroCentrifuge&r turns it into a &aCrystal",
    "",
    "Non-metal ores use &eLTXI&r's own items at each step.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Only the &aGrinder&r works out of the box. The other four need their &bOre Processing&r upgrade module, then &bOre Processing&r selected in the recipe mode screen. The HydroSieve's module is a crafting recipe, the Voltaic Injector and Chem Lab modules need Precision Circuits, and the ElectroCentrifuge's Ore Crystallizing Tubes need a Nano-Core Processor. Smelt the Shards until then.",
    "",
    "Every stage item smelts, metals into one ingot and non-metals into the finished item.",
    "",
    "Each metal stage, the Grinder included, gives one item plus a 50% chance of a second, so a raw ore averages 7.6 &aCrystals&r and at best 32. Non-metal ores get a flat two at the Grinder, about 10 on average. Vanilla ones like diamond need the ore block, so use &bSilk Touch&r.",
  ],
  "quest.680B3A82D8AF9950.quest_desc": [
    "Your first guns come out of the &dFabricator&r on &3Enhanced Circuits&r, well before the turrets. &aSerenity&r shreds at close range, makes no sculk vibrations, and its hits don't anger neutral mobs, which makes it the sidearm for the Deep Dark. &aMirage&r trades that for more than twice the range and harder hits.",
    "",
    "The &aWayfinder&r is the odd one out. It launches glowsticks that fly through mobs and stick to any block face they hit, underwater included, so you can light a cave from the entrance.",
    "",
    "All three reload from their own charge. Keep them topped up in an &aEnergy Cell Array&r's charging slots, and don't reload early, because a reload costs the same charge however many shots are left.",
  ],
  "quest.12991E755825749C.title": "&aBattery Acid",
  "quest.21C4EB4528C091CA.quest_desc": [
    "The &aGeo Synthesizer&r makes stone-related blocks water and lava.",
    "",
    "Put one block of the stone type you want in its slot as a pattern and feed it both fluids. Neither the block nor the fluids are used up for most stones, so it never stops. Obsidian is the exception and uses lava.",
  ],
  "quest.6EDEAB6EB8C352F6.quest_desc": [
    "The Grinder is only the first step of the ore chain. The &aHydroSieve&r and &2Voltaic Injector&r are the next two.",
    "",
    "Build both. The &aHydroSieve&r washes Dirty Dust into Clumps with water, and the Voltaic Injector energizes Clumps into Chunks. Each step has another 50% chance at an extra item.",
    "",
    "The &2Voltaic Injector&r is also where Tungsten and Pyroxene come from later, so send every ore through it.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: The Injector takes Slatesteel Plates, so it waits on the Material Press.",
  ],
  "quest.3E7C6BF63D71A56A.title": "Heavy Weapons",
  "quest.2E5E8A019A56881E.title": "Assembler",
  "quest.2689B0928FA18765.title": "Nova 77/HX",
  "quest.6D7ED2315F9E93BD.quest_desc": [
    "The &aMedium Voltaic Cell&r is one of the big progression points in &eLTXI&r, as it lets you craft the tier 3 &dPrecision Circuits&r used in more advanced weapons, machinery and upgrades.",
    "",
    "Its &aPolymer Bars&r start in the Grinder, which turns bamboo or sugar cane into Resinous Biomass. The Mixer finishes them with water and Sulfuric Acid.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: Once you have Fluoropolymer, the Assembler makes two cells per craft from it instead of one.",
  ],
  "quest.19019EBBF6A8CD45.quest_desc": [
    "The &dPrecision Circuit&r is the tier 3 progression blocker, allowing you to make defensive turrets, better tools and weapons, the &6Atmospheric Scrubber&r, the &3Bio/ARU Garden&r and the Auto Fabricator.",
  ],
  "quest.31053F968B050ADE.title": "Repair Station",
  "quest.4382135A655314AF.title": "Mixer",
  "quest.677539F514A6986B.title": "Spark Fruit",
  "quest.5EF4EC94EEE9FCDB.title": "&6Nano-Core Processor",
  "quest.3E3BDECE4FC4283C.quest_desc": [
    "The &dFabricator&r makes the &6Atmospheric Scrubber&r, the &3Bio/ARU Garden&r and the turrets, as well as equipment and upgrades.",
    "",
    "The &3Upgrade Station&r allows you to slot upgrades into your equipment. Machines can be directly upgraded in their interface. The station also has a &aLight Colors&r button for recoloring the glow on ε-Series tools and weapons.",
  ],
  "quest.54BECF70662E7965.quest_desc": [
    "The hardest part of the next processor to find is &2Pyroxene&r, and it only comes from olivine.",
    "",
    "Run &2Raw Olivine&r through the ore chain. Each Washed Olivine the &2Voltaic Injector&r energizes has a 7.5% chance to drop Pyroxene, and a &aNano Logic Core&r needs eight. The rest is two Logic Cores, Niobium Dust and 4,000 mB of Argon in the &2Arc Furnace&r.",
  ],
  "quest.680B3A82D8AF9950.title": "Lightweight Weapons",
  "quest.18D0822972C250BA.title": "Elite Circuit Board",
  "quest.2618CDD301362A21.quest_desc": [
    "&eLTXI&r adds digital versions of Minecraft's 3 smelt blocks: &aDigital Furnace&r, &2Digital Smoker&r, and Digital Blast Furnace.",
  ],
  "quest.0E59D4359DA75B3D.quest_desc": [
    "Everything past the &dPrecision Circuit&r is built from gases, and the &aAtmospheric Scrubber&r is how you get them. It pulls them out of the air, or out of the water and lava around it, depending on its mode and where it stands.",
    "",
    "Build one and set it running. Before long you'll want one in each of these spots:",
    "",
    "- &aMethane&r: Localized Gases, in a swamp.",
    "- &2Nitrogen&r: Ambient Gases, anywhere in the Overworld.",
    "- &aSulphurine&r: Ambient Gases, in the Nether.",
    "- &2Argon&r: Ambient Gases, in the End. It's the only source.",
    "- &aSea Water&r: Localized Fluids, waterlogged in an ocean.",
    "",
    "&o&7For storage simplicity, these gases behave as fluids and can be stored in tanks and fluid drives.",
  ],
  "quest.7FD632909226FFEB.title": "Arc Furnace and Slatesteel",
  "quest.62C16C9468193F6C.title": "ElectroCentrifuge",
  "task.0D25DA6D98413994.title": "Ore Processing Chain",
  "quest.3D3AD363723B756C.quest_desc": [
    "Medium Voltaic Cells carried you through the Precision tier. The next processor needs a &aHigh-Energy Voltaic Cell&r.",
    "",
    "Assemble one now, and plan for more. A single Real Virtuality Processor uses seven of them, counting the ones inside its four Nano-Core Processors.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: Each cell takes 16 &2Sodium Dust&r, so your Spark Fruit supply matters again. A Bio/ARU Garden can grow them.",
  ],
  "quest.7A727FA32BD3EF53.quest_desc": [
    "Once you've found some titanium, you'll want to start crafting the &aBasic Circuits&r used for basic machinery.",
    "",
    "Almost every machine can be upgraded in some way that improves or changes its functionality, this menu can be accessed via the top-right tab of any machine interface.",
  ],
  "quest.31053F968B050ADE.quest_desc": [
    "ε and Wonderland gear runs on energy, but everything else you own still wears out.",
    "",
    "The &aRepair Station&r restores durability on any normal tool, weapon or armor piece using power, as many times as you like. Just bring it in before it breaks.",
  ],
  "task.7B7309698598EF21.title": "Turrets",
  "quest.2BDF212C585D1A2C.title": "Ore Processing Chain",
  "quest.62C16C9468193F6C.quest_desc": [
    "The &aElectroCentrifuge&r breaks down items into other pieces. Its recipe mode is set with the upper button on the bottom-left of the interface.",
    "",
    "For now, set it to &2Element Extraction&r to obtain Oxygen from flint, sand, quartz, or water, which you'll use to make Slatesteel in the next quest.",
  ],
  "quest.05840D6E05F68B73.quest_desc": [
    "The &aChem Lab&r runs reactions between items and fluids, and later recipes like Fluoropolymer, Silicone Rubber and Elite Circuit Boards all go through it.",
    "",
    "It can be used as part of &eLTXI's&r ore processing chain, or to process chemicals in higher progression tiers.",
  ],
  "quest.15BC82FEDC344BEE.quest_desc": [
    "There is no tungsten ore. All of it comes out of your titanium ore processing.",
    "",
    "When the &2Voltaic Injector&r energizes a Titanium Clump into a Chunk, it has a 1% chance to drop &aTungsten Trioxide&r. Two of those, a Slatesteel Dust and Hydrogen make the dust in the Chem Lab, and the &2Arc Furnace&r finishes it with Nitrogen into &aTungsten-Plated Slatesteel&r.",
    "",
    "The Hanabi, the Noctis turret and the Daybreak all take it by the stack, and the &6Feed The Beast&r challenge asks for it in Arc Alloys.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: At 1%, one ingot costs about 200 Titanium Clumps. Send every Titanium Ore you mine through the full chain from now on instead of smelting it.",
  ],
  "quest.7FD632909226FFEB.quest_desc": [
    "An &aArc Furnace&r lets you combine several materials or metals into one stronger alloy, and it smelts dusts that a normal furnace cannot handle.",
    "",
    "One of the most important alloys in &eLTXI&r is &2Slatesteel&r. To craft it, you'll need &2Oxygen&r from the ElectroCentrifuge on &3Element Extraction&r.",
  ],
  "quest.45B06D8A03232CF8.quest_desc": [
    "&eLTXI&r's last circuit is also its most expensive part. One &aReal Virtuality Processor&r takes four Nano-Core Processors, eight Rhenium Ingots and 24 Echo Serum.",
    "",
    "Build it in the &2Fabricator&r, which charges 100M FE for this one. The Nova, the Infernal Lava Tank and the rank 5 upgrades all need it.",
    "",
    "The &6Feed The Beast&r challenge asks for one too, in Feed the Factories.",
  ],
  "quest.4BFCCA0C7FA49C28.quest_desc": [
    "Reaching Tier 3 Progression allows you to craft the main &aε-Series tools&r (sword, axe, drill, shovel and hoe), stationary defense turrets, and heavier ranged weapons.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Check the \", {\"text\": \"Tools\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,ltxi:guide,ltxi:tools.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Tools page in the LTXI GuideMe\"}}, \", \", {\"text\": \"Turrets\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,ltxi:guide,ltxi:turrets/index.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Turrets page in the LTXI GuideMe\"}}, \" and \", {\"text\": \"Weapons\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,ltxi:guide,ltxi:weapons/index.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Weapons page in the LTXI GuideMe\"}}, \" GuideMe pages for more details.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.507B07726C49351E.title": "Auto Fabricator",
  "quest.359C9BCF250CA832.quest_desc": [
    "&eLTX Industries&r (&eLTXI&r) is a sci-fi tech mod that adds machines, weapons, tools, and a variety of resources and upgrades.",
    "",
    "To get started with &eLTXI&r, you'll want to find some titanium by mining underground.",
  ],
  "quest.677539F514A6986B.quest_desc": [
    "The &aSpark Fruit&r generates on the underside of jungle leaves, but they can also be bought from farmer villagers or wandering traders.",
    "",
    "Mature fruits emit light so foraging for them at night makes finding them much easier. Each mature one drops 3 fruits, affected by the Fortune enchantment.",
    "",
    "Their main use in &eLTXI&r is being ground down into &2Sodium Dust&r.",
  ],
  "quest.7A727FA32BD3EF53.title": "First Circuits and Power",
  "quest.27E8B6B7A21D31D7.title": "Bathyal Water Tank",
  "quest.660A89B05AEBBDBA.quest_desc": [
    "The built-in energy buffers in your machines won't carry you far, so before the tech tree opens up you need a generator.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aPortable Generator&r. It burns any furnace fuel for 64 FE per tick, and it runs anywhere, even underwater.",
    "",
    "Fuel is stored in its gauge as Fuel Units first, one for every 100 ticks of burn time, and each unit is worth 2,500 FE. A piece of &2Coal&r becomes 16 units, or 40,000 FE.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: Partly used units are tracked and the generator never makes more energy than it can store in its 100,000 FE buffer, so no fuel is wasted when it sits full.",
  ],
  "quest.6EDEAB6EB8C352F6.title": "Ore Processing Machines",
  "quest.3E7C6BF63D71A56A.quest_desc": [
    "Tier 4 adds the two heaviest things in the armory, and both are built on Tungsten-Plated Slatesteel.",
    "",
    "The &2Noctis A/DS Turret&r guards an area on its own. The &aDaybreak 41/RL&r is the one you carry, and at 100M FE in the &2Fabricator&r it's the most expensive thing you'll have built so far.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Check the \", {\"text\": \"Noctis\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,ltxi:guide,ltxi:turrets/railgun_turret.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Noctis page in the LTXI GuideMe\"}}, \" and \", {\"text\": \"Daybreak\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,ltxi:guide,ltxi:weapons/daybreak.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Daybreak page in the LTXI GuideMe\"}}, \" GuideMe pages for range, damage and ammo.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.3E3BDECE4FC4283C.title": "Fabricating and Installing Upgrades",
  "quest.06354FA695904AFD.title": "Material Press",
  "quest.660A89B05AEBBDBA.title": "Early Generation",
  "quest.05840D6E05F68B73.title": "Chem Lab",
  "quest.4BFCCA0C7FA49C28.title": "Tools, Turrets, \\&\\ Weapons",
  "quest.27E8B6B7A21D31D7.quest_desc": [
    "Most of your Chem Lab recipes start with water. The &aBathyal Water Tank&r is a Portable Tank that never runs dry.",
    "",
    "It's an &2Assembler&r recipe that takes 2,500,000 mB of water during the craft, so pipe it in from a real water source rather than a stack of buckets.",
  ],
  "quest.3EEF7169EA2EE7F2.quest_desc": [
    "&aVitriol Berries&r grow on &2Bilevines&r hanging under the ceilings of Nether Fortresses and Bastion Remnants. Use a vine with berries to pick them, and plant a berry under any solid block to start your own; bone meal on an empty vine grows a berry on the spot.",
    "",
    "Its primary use is being broken down into &2Acidic Biomass&r which makes &aSulfuric Acid&r when mixed with water.",
  ],
  "quest.19019EBBF6A8CD45.title": "Precision Circuit",
  "quest.781E24BC6FCF69AF.title": "Noble Gas",
  "quest.3CB6C9F3F4A205E3.quest_desc": [
    "The &aInfernal Lava Tank&r is the lava version of the Bathyal tank, a Portable Tank that never empties.",
    "",
    "On top of a Real Virtuality Processor and Tungsten and Rhenium Plates, the craft takes 10,000,000 mB of lava. A single Scrubber with no upgrades on Ambient Fluids in the Nether would need over 80 hours to make that, so fill it from your biggest lava source.",
  ],
  "quest.45B06D8A03232CF8.title": "&dReal Virtuality Processor",
  "quest.15BC82FEDC344BEE.title": "Tungsten-Plated Slatesteel",
  "quest.1BD6D491EEC018D0.title": "Wonderland Armor",
  "quest.5B01DB41B229C43D.quest_desc": [
    "Methane and Chlorine have a second use. With &2Silicon Dust&r the Chem Lab turns them into Silicone Oil, and a second pass with Sulphurine sets it into &aSilicone Rubber&r.",
    "",
    "Make a stack. A full Wonderland suit takes 24, and the Bathyal Water Tank takes 32.",
  ],
  "quest.3EEF7169EA2EE7F2.title": "Vitriol Berries",
  "quest.5B01DB41B229C43D.title": "Silicone Rubber",
  "task.6FAC0C6B14AE1494.title": "Digital Smelters",
  "quest.54BECF70662E7965.title": "Nano Logic Core",
  "quest.3CB6C9F3F4A205E3.title": "Infernal Lava Tank",
  "quest.3D3AD363723B756C.title": "High-Energy Voltaic Cell",
  "quest.1BD3EA2ADBDA309B.quest_desc": [
    "&aGloom Shrooms&r grow in the Deep Dark and nowhere else. Bring the Serenity, since it doesn't wake the Warden.",
    "",
    "Pick some and mix two with Sulfuric Acid into &aEcho Serum&r. The Real Virtuality Processor takes 24 of it, which is 48 shrooms per processor.",
    "",
    "A &2Bio/ARU Garden&r grows more from one shroom and Ammonia, so you only have to make the trip once.",
  ],
  "task.3518AFC8391600B4.title": "Weapons",
  "quest.18D0822972C250BA.quest_desc": [
    "Every circuit so far has had its own board. The &aElite Circuit Board&r replaces all of them.",
    "",
    "Make one in the &2Chem Lab&r. The Nano-Core Processor needs two, and you'll want a steady supply after that.",
    "",
    "It also opens a cheaper route in the &2Assembler&r. Once you have &2Logic Cores&r, one Elite Board, a plate and one or two Logic Cores make four Basic, two Enhanced or two Precision Circuits in a single craft.",
  ],
  "quest.59E5B7EF32280569.quest_desc": [
    "The &3Bio/ARU Garden&r is a self-contained greenhouse. Put a plant in it, give it water and energy, and it grows copies without using up the original.",
    "",
    "In this pack it also grows &eMystical Agriculture&r seeds into essence, so one Garden per seed makes a compact essence farm.",
    "",
    "Spark Fruit, Chorus Fruit and Gloom Shrooms grow in it too, and all three feed the late-game circuits.",
  ],
  "quest.5E72E067E7C37D7D.title": "Niobium",
  "quest.0E59D4359DA75B3D.title": "Atmospheric Scrubber",
}